# Testing and Lint Gates

- Before closing a task, run at least one relevant check for the changed scope (for example lint, typecheck, build, or tests).
- New behavior should have a clear verification path (automated test when practical, otherwise a short manual QA note).
- For small UI or copy-only changes, lightweight verification is acceptable.
- For bug fixes, add regression coverage when the effort is reasonable.
- If a check fails and is temporarily deferred, document the reason and a follow-up.
- Prefer deterministic tests and avoid flaky timing-based assertions.
- For critical flows (auth, billing, data mutations), increase confidence with broader validation when possible.
- Update docs or inline usage notes when behavior or developer workflow changes.
